  "status": "candidate record. The homepage replaces R3's history, authority and leadership-dividend chapters with the three /new-age-leadership chapters: the organisation changing shape, what this feels like in practice, and what your AI Brain makes possible with the returned hour.",
  "scopeRequested": "Krish, 2026-09-25, with screenshots of the three /new-age-leadership sections (\"The organisation changes shape.\", \"The system does not replace your judgement. It brings more to it.\" and \"What your AI Brain makes possible\" beside \"The returned hour\"): \"these 3 sections in new-age-leadership should be used on the homepage instead of the 3 sections that are currently there, the existing sections should be scrapped.\"",
  "sessionDecisions": [
    "The three sections are carried whole, as /new-age-leadership has them, including each one's first state: the reach sequence opens on \"The feeling is familiar. The reach is new.\" before \"The organisation changes shape.\", and the practice sequence runs Notice, Connect, Prepare.",
    "One source for both pages: src/components/leadership-chapters/leadershipChapters.ts owns the three chapters' markup and scroll behaviour. /new-age-leadership renders from it and its prerendered HTML is unchanged apart from asset hashes and aria-hidden on its four decorative chapter films.",
    "The homepage generator (scripts/qa/build-homepage-release.mjs) cuts the three R3 chapters from the immutable R3 source's markup, runtime and styles by named anchors that fail the build if missing, and inserts the shared chapters between the opening and the route. The R3 source itself is untouched. The skip link now targets the new chapters.",
    "The R3 pin controller (pinnedChapters.ts/.css) and its lifecycle test are retired; the new chapters pin with their own R5 sticky tracks, as on /new-age-leadership. Reduced motion keeps the pins and drops transitions and films, which is that page's approved policy.",
    "Homepage-only integration: the chapters pin under the homepage's fixed masthead (66px, 64px on a phone) and take its gutter (4.4vw, 5.13vw at 700px and below). Below 900px two R5 rules (a flat 16px phone padding and a stale flex justify-content on what is now a grid) put the reach copy off that edge; the homepage corrects both.",
    "The homepage scroll contract now declares reach (2 states) and benefits (6) at 1440x900 and 390x844, and practice (3) at 1440x900 only, since below 900px the practice scenes flow one after another by design."
  ],
